+        <article id="journal-article" class="journal-content">
+          <p>
+            Every memorable cup at The Daily Grind begins long before our roasters fire up the drum. Our sourcing philosophy is built on multi-year, direct-trade relationships with smallholder farmers and cooperatives across high-altitude micro-regions in Colombia's Huila department, Ethiopia's Yirgacheffe highlands, and the volcanic slopes of Antigua, Guatemala. By bypassing traditional commodity brokers and negotiating directly at origin, we guarantee farm-gate prices that sit at least 40% above Fair Trade minimums—ensuring growers can reinvest in soil health, fair wages for seasonal pickers, and local community infrastructure.
+          </p>
+          <p>
+            Altitude and biodiversity play a decisive role in developing complex flavor precursors inside the coffee cherry. We partner exclusively with farms practicing shade-grown, regenerative agriculture at elevations between 1,500 and 2,100 meters above sea level. Under canopies of native inga, banana, and citrus trees, coffee cherries mature more slowly during cool mountain nights, concentrating natural sugars and organic acids. During harvest season, pickers make multiple passes through each parcel to hand-select only deep-crimson, peak-ripeness cherries, leaving under-ripe fruit on the branch to mature for later collection.
+          </p>
+          <p>
+            Once harvested, the cherries undergo meticulous post-harvest processing tailored to each varietal and local microclimate. In water-rich highland mills, our washed lots are depulped within eight hours of picking, fermented in ceramic-tiled tanks for 24 to 36 hours to achieve vibrant citrus clarity, and dried slowly on raised African beds. For our seasonal honey and natural lots, whole or partially mucilage-coated cherries are turned hourly on sunny patios for up to three weeks, imparting lush notes of wild berry, stone fruit, and raw cacao into the green seed.
+          </p>
+          <p>
+            Before any harvest leaves origin, our quality team conducts rigorous blind cuppings alongside the producers, scoring every micro-lot on fragrance, acidity, body, sweetness, and clean finish—selecting only coffees that score 86 points or higher on the Specialty Coffee Association scale. The green beans are then vacuum-sealed in GrainPro hermetic liners to lock in moisture equilibrium during ocean transit. Once they arrive at our roastery, we test-roast small batches to map out a custom thermal profile that honors the farmer's craft in every single pour.
+          </p>
+        </article>
